// The particle sprites and the budgets of the effects.
//
// The original keeps the look and the forces of its particles in seven shared pools that its
// bursts and emitters spawn into (pools.flecs and curves.flecs of the original). Box gives every
// layer of an effect its own, so each layer in this folder carries the settings of the pool the
// original fires it into:
//
// | Pool   | Sprite    | Blend    | Gravity | Drag | Turbulence | Soft | Lit  | Curves                 |
// | ------ | --------- | -------- | ------- | ---- | ---------- | ---- | ---- | ---------------------- |
// | fx     | sprPuff   | alpha    | 5 down  | 2.5  | 0.7 at 1.2 | 0.35 | 0.8  | puff, ease out alpha   |
// | glow   | sprSpark  | additive | 4 down  | 1.5  |            | 0.25 | 0    | taper, ease out alpha  |
// | smoke  | sprPuff   | alpha    | 0.6     | 0.9  | 1.5 at 0.55| 0.5  | 0.85 | swell, smoke fade      |
// | trail  | sprPuff   | alpha    | 0.35 up | 1.4  | 0.9 at 0.7 | 0.5  | 0.9  | swell, smoke fade      |
// | fire   | sprFlare  | additive | 1.6 up  | 3    | 2.2 at 1.4 | 0.6  | 0    | flare, spike           |
// | debris | sprChunk  | alpha    | 17 down | 0.3  |            |      | 1    | ease in alpha          |
// | ember  | sprSpark  | additive | 0.8 up  | 1.1  | 1.8 at 1.1 | 0.25 | 0    | taper, ember fade      |
//
// A layer's ParticleCurves sample at the keys 0, 1/3, 2/3 and 1 of the life what the original
// computes per particle: the size curve of the pool times the growth of the burst (size + grow *
// age over its mean life), the alpha of the color ramp times the alpha curve and envelope of the
// pool (the start key skips a fade in of a few hundredths of the life), and the colors of the
// ramp as multipliers of the layer's color in linear light. The original's emissive strengths
// (glow 1.6, fire 2.6, ember 2.2), its brightness variance, the squash of a stretch below 1, the
// mass of debris and turbulence_speed have no equivalent and are left out; a stretch above 1
// becomes ParticleAppearance.stretch at the layer's typical speed, half its initial one. The
// layers that look clearly weaker without the emission have an additive halo layer.

using box.texture
using box.particle

// The soft round puff of dust and smoke
sprPuff {
  TexturePath: {path: "apps/oreelse/etc/assets/particles/puff.svg", width: 256, height: 256}
}

// The bright flare of fire and of the halos
sprFlare {
  TexturePath: {path: "apps/oreelse/etc/assets/particles/flare.svg", width: 256, height: 256}
}

// The small hot spark of glints, sparks and embers
sprSpark {
  TexturePath: {path: "apps/oreelse/etc/assets/particles/spark.svg", width: 128, height: 128}
}

// The rock chunk of debris
sprChunk {
  TexturePath: {path: "apps/oreelse/etc/assets/particles/chunk.svg", width: 64, height: 64}
}

// The budgets for a late game base, the original's stress test mode: a ring of some 90 gun,
// laser and missile turrets whose every shot plays sparks and a puff or dust, a wave of critters
// dying in combusts and splats, missiles exploding, rockets launching and the presses of two
// factories. A template plays at most 64 times at once, about what the original's pools hold
// (its glow pool of 512 fits some 50 spark bursts), and all of them together 640 times. Past a
// budget a burst that no view sees, or that lies more than 80 units from the camera, is
// dropped, and one in view replays the play of its template that has played longest.
$ {
  ParticleSettings: {
    effect_max: 64,
    effect_total: 640,
    effect_overflow: EffectSkip,
    effect_distance: 80
  }
}
